@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #fcfcfd
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam arrowColor #0f172a
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #fff7d6
skinparam noteBorderColor #b45309
skinparam noteFontColor #334155
skinparam roundcorner 16
title Activity - filestorage/MountTarget
skinparam activity {
  backgroundColor #f8fafc
  borderColor #0f172a
  fontColor #0f172a
  diamondBackgroundColor #e2e8f0
  diamondBorderColor #1d4ed8
  diamondFontColor #0f172a
  startColor #1d4ed8
  endColor #0f172a
  barColor #1d4ed8
}
start
partition "Observe and Bind" {
:Start from shared flow\nshared/diagrams/shared-reconcile-activity.svg;
:Read desired MountTarget spec, tracked status,\nand delete intent;
if ("Tracked or explicit OCI identity present?") then (yes)
:Get the current OCI resource via\nGetMountTarget;
else (no)
:Resolve an existing OCI resource through\nListMountTargets using filters\navailabilityDomain, compartmentId, displayName;
:Create the OCI resource via CreateMountTarget\nwhen no reusable match is found;
:Persist the resolved or created OCI identity\ninto status;
endif
}
if ("Delete requested?") then (yes)
partition "Delete" {
:Delete path uses DeleteMountTarget with\nrequired via GetMountTarget or\nListMountTargets to DELETED confirmation;
:Confirm deletion via GetMountTarget or\nListMountTargets until OCI reaches DELETED;
if ("Delete cleanup and finalizer release succeed?") then (yes)
:Remove the finalizer after delete completion;
else (no)
:Stay blocked until cleanup or finalizer\nrelease succeeds;
endif
}
stop
else (no)
partition "Lifecycle Classification" {
if ("OCI state in retryable set?") then (yes)
:Request requeue while OCI remains in CREATING,\nDELETING;
stop
endif
if ("OCI state is outside success targets?") then (yes)
:Return an unsuccessful reconcile result until\nOCI reaches ACTIVE, FAILED;
stop
endif
}
partition "Ready and Drift Handling" {
:Compare live OCI state against the\nrepo-authored mutation surface;
if ("Force-new or conflicting drift detected?") then (yes)
:Reject drift before OCI mutation for force-new\nfields availabilityDomain, compartmentId,\nsubnetId, hostnameLabel (+1 more);
stop
endif
if ("Supported mutable drift detected?") then (yes)
:Apply CancelDowngradeShapeMountTarget,\nChangeMountTargetCompartment,\nScheduleDowngradeShapeMountTarget (+2 more)\nonly for mutable fields displayName,\nfreeformTags, definedTags, nsgIds (+1 more);
else (no)
:Skip the no-op mutation path;
endif
:Run provider helper hooks\ncreate=tfresource.CreateResource,\ntfresource.WaitForCreatedState;\nupdate=tfresource.UpdateResource,\ntfresource.WaitForUpdatedState;\ndelete=tfresource.DeleteResource when the\nmatching field-driven path executes;
:Apply explicit follow-up semantics\ncreate=read-after-write;\nupdate=read-after-write; delete=confirm-delete;
:Return success for the ACTIVE, FAILED success\nstate;
:Project required status and finalizer policy\nretain-until-confirmed-delete;
:Requeue on provisioning, updating, terminating;
}
endif
stop
note right
shared diagram:
shared/diagrams/shared-reconcile-activity.svg
Start from the shared reconcile activity and
specialize provider-backed CRUD, wait, and
status-projection details here.
Controller-local activity diagrams add
list-lookup hints, secret policies, delete
handling, and open formal gaps.
archetype batch: Generated service-manager
controllers specialize the shared reconcile path
with formal runtime ownership.
service: filestorage
slug: mounttarget
kind: MountTarget
archetype: generated-service-manager
status/finalizer: required /
retain-until-confirmed-delete
requeue: provisioning, updating, terminating
provider states: create CREATING; update none;
delete DELETING
follow-up: create=read-after-write;
update=read-after-write; delete=confirm-delete
supported drift: displayName, freeformTags,
definedTags, nsgIds (+1 more)
reject before mutate: force-new fields
availabilityDomain, compartmentId, subnetId,
hostnameLabel (+1 more)
create-only fields: none
list lookup: oci_file_storage_mount_targets
filters availabilityDomain, compartmentId,
displayName; Adopt only a unique mount target in
the requested availability domain and
compartment.
conflicts: none
open gaps: none
CREATING and UPDATING requeue, ACTIVE succeeds,
FAILED is terminal, and delete retains the
finalizer through DELETING until DELETED or
absence.
The generated status projects exportSetId and
private-IP identities needed by dependent
exports.
Display name, tags, NSGs, and security
attributes update in place; placement, subnet,
hostname, and chosen IP require replacement.
The runtime has no Kubernetes Secret side
effects.
end note
@enduml
